icación determinista de tareas agénticas"}},{"id":"README.md#99","metadata":{"content":"cada uno)","okf_concept":"README.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"TASK.md — Verificación determinista de tareas agénticas"}},{"id":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md#0","metadata":{"content":"# TASK.md — Especificación (borrador v0.1)\n\n> Hermano de ejecución de la familia **design.md / game.md / ccdd**.\n> Mismo ADN: documento de dos capas (YAML máquina-checable + Markdown humano)\n> con una capa de validación determinista que es la fuente de verdad, no la prosa.\n>\n> Objeto que gobierna: **¿la tarea delegada logró su objetivo?** — respondido por\n> gates deterministas contra el sistema real, no por la opinión del modelo ejecutor.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Principio rector (heredado de ccdd)\n\n> *\"Lo verificable va a un gate determinista; lo opinable va a una persona — el modelo informa, no decide.\"*","okf_concept":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"TASK.md — Especificación (borrador v0.1)"}},{"id":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md#1","metadata":{"content":"una persona — el modelo informa, no decide.\"*\n\nCorolario operativo (cierre con la economía de modelos):\n**el contrato declara HECHOS (post-condiciones), no COMPORTAMIENTO.** Por eso el\nejecutor puede ser cualquier modelo: el gate checa hechos, no cómo se llegó a ellos.\n`facts-not-behavior` (game.md) = independencia del modelo.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Modelo conceptual: Historia + AC + DoD\n\n| Concepto ágil | En el contrato | Régimen |\n|---|---|---|\n| Narrativa (\"Como… quiero… para…\") | cuerpo Markdown | blando / juicio humano |\n| **Acceptance Criteria** (por historia) | gates deterministas específicos | duro |\n| **Definition of Done** (transversal) | set de gates reusable (`DOD.md`) | duro |\n\n**Booleano de compleción:**","okf_concept":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"TASK.md — Especificación (borrador v0.1)"}},{"id":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md#10","metadata":{"content":"natural.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Front-matter: campos","okf_concept":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"TASK.md — Especificación (borrador v0.1)"}},{"id":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md#100","metadata":{"content":"tract-lint (starter, v0.1)","okf_concept":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"TASK.md — Especificación (borrador v0.1)"}},{"id":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md#101","metadata":{"content":"ract-lint (starter, v0.1)","okf_concept":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"TASK.md — Especificación (borrador v0.1)"}},{"id":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md#102","metadata":{"content":"act-lint (starter, v0.1)","okf_concept":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"TASK.md — Especificación (borrador v0.1)"}},{"id":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md#103","metadata":{"content":"ct-lint (starter, v0.1)","okf_concept":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"TASK.md — Especificación (borrador v0.1)"}},{"id":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md#104","metadata":{"content":"t-lint (starter, v0.1)","okf_concept":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"TASK.md — Especificación (borrador v0.1)"}},{"id":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md#105","metadata":{"content":"-lint (starter, v0.1)","okf_concept":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"TASK.md — Especificación (borrador v0.1)"}},{"id":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md#106","metadata":{"content":"lint (starter, v0.1)","okf_concept":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"TASK.md — Especificación (borrador v0.1)"}},{"id":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md#107","metadata":{"content":"int (starter, v0.1)","okf_concept":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"TASK.md — Especificación (borrador v0.1)"}},{"id":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md#108","metadata":{"content":"nt (starter, v0.1)","okf_concept":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"TASK.md — Especificación (borrador v0.1)"}},{"id":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md#109","metadata":{"content":"t (starter, v0.1)","okf_concept":"taskmd_spec_v0.1.md",